Isolated 2026-08-22: not in use.

colcon skips any package directory containing this file, so aries_vision_grasp is not
built, not installed, and not on the environment's path. Nothing is deleted --
delete this file and rebuild to bring it back.

Before isolating, the one thing outside these three packages that needed
aries_vision_grasp was aries_bringup's camera_downlink.py, which imported
NumpyImageBridge (cv_bridge segfaults under NumPy 2.x, so every image node
uses it). That module moved to aries_common/image_bridge.py and all five
importers now take it from there, so the downlink no longer depends on
anything isolated here.

Still pointing at aries_vision_grasp, and therefore dead while this file
exists: aries_hardware.launch.py's enable_yolo_debug:=true node, and
scripts/vision/*. enable_yolo_debug defaults to false, so the normal launch
path is unaffected.
